WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.337
Welcome to Explore ChatGPT, from AI Confidence Academy.

00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:15.844
In this short walkthrough, we will explore two ways to use your voice: dictation, and a spoken conversation.

00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:18.346
You do not need special language.

00:00:18.346 --> 00:00:22.100
Start with something you want help understanding or organizing.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:27.795
Dictation turns what you say into text that you can review before sending.

00:00:27.795 --> 00:00:33.490
A voice conversation lets you speak with ChatGPT and hear a spoken response.

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.243
These are different controls.

00:00:35.243 --> 00:00:40.500
Their appearance and location can vary by device, app version, and account.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.134
For dictation, look for the microphone control in the message box.

00:00:45.134 --> 00:00:48.083
Allow microphone access if your device asks.

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:49.768
Speak one clear request.

00:00:49.768 --> 00:00:54.823
For example: Help me organize three things I need to accomplish today.

00:00:54.823 --> 00:01:00.300
I need to buy groceries, make a phone call, and tidy my desk.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.380
Finish the recording using the control shown on your screen.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.420
Read the text that appears.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.868
Did it capture your words correctly?

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:12.948
Correct a name, remove a detail, or add something important.

00:01:12.948 --> 00:01:14.580
Then send the message.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:20.700
Dictation gives you the convenience of speaking while keeping a chance to check your request.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.147
For a spoken conversation, choose the Voice control instead.

00:01:24.147 --> 00:01:26.828
It may look like a sound wave.

00:01:26.828 --> 00:01:30.274
If asked, allow microphone access and choose a voice.

00:01:30.274 --> 00:01:32.189
Ask the same everyday question.

00:01:32.189 --> 00:01:38.700
Listen to the response, and remember that a confident sounding voice can still give an incorrect answer.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.474
Keep participating.

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:41.796
You could say: Make that simpler.

00:01:41.796 --> 00:01:43.730
Let's start with just one.

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:46.826
Or: Ask me one question at a time.

00:01:46.826 --> 00:01:50.309
You can ask a follow-up or interrupt to clarify.

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:53.017
Your purpose and judgment guide the conversation.

00:01:53.017 --> 00:01:56.500
You do not have to accept the first suggestion.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.316
Use the microphone control to mute yourself when needed.

00:02:00.316 --> 00:02:04.980
Use the end or stop voice control when you are finished.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.220
Avoid speaking private information that the task does not need.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.308
If Voice is unavailable, check microphone permissions and your account's feature availability.

00:02:14.308 --> 00:02:17.700
Dictation and typing remain separate options where available.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.213
Now try one small task in your own words.

00:02:21.213 --> 00:02:22.774
Describe what you need.

00:02:22.774 --> 00:02:25.116
Review or listen to the response.

00:02:25.116 --> 00:02:27.458
Then ask for one useful change.

00:02:27.458 --> 00:02:29.800
Check any important facts before acting.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:30.971
People come first.

00:02:30.971 --> 00:02:32.532
AI is the tool.

00:02:32.532 --> 00:02:34.093
Confidence is the product.

00:02:34.093 --> 00:02:37.216
Thank you for learning with AI Confidence Academy.
